# Sun Pool & Spa Supply — client redirect rules
# Appended to dist/_redirects during hydrate. Never hand-edit dist/_redirects;
# it is overwritten on every build.
#
# Every source path below was confirmed to return 200 on the live SiteGround site
# on 2026-07-29 (curl -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}'). None are guessed. The /hp/
# subpaths were found by crawling the legacy homepage nav, not assumed.

# Sun Pool carries no saunas, so SAUNAS_URL points the nav at the match quiz.
# The category page is still built, so anyone holding the old URL would land on
# an empty grid without this rule (TVD-052). /saunas/ 404s on the legacy site, so
# this rule is forward-looking only, not a legacy 301.
/saunas/ /quiz/ 301
/saunas /quiz/ 301

# Legacy category pages. Titled "Hot Tubs" and "Hydropool Swim Spas" on the old
# site and linked from its homepage nav, so these carry real ranking. They must
# precede the /hp/ rules below: _redirects matches top-down, and a bare /hp/ rule
# does NOT match /hp/hot-tubs/ — Cloudflare matches exact paths unless splatted.
/hp/hot-tubs/ /hot-tubs/ 301
/hp/hot-tubs /hot-tubs/ 301
/hp/swim-spas/ /swim-spas/ 301
/hp/swim-spas /swim-spas/ 301

# The /hp/ index itself was the old landing page, so it goes to the homepage. This
# must stay ABOVE the splat: /hp/* also matches /hp/ with an empty splat, and
# _redirects takes the first match, which would otherwise send it to inventory.
/hp/ / 301
/hp / 301

# Anything else under the legacy /hp/ tree goes to the inventory grid, which is
# the closest equivalent of what that section was for.
/hp/* /active-inventory/ 301

# Remaining legacy URLs, all confirmed 200 on the old site. /privacy-policy/
# needs no rule — the new site serves that exact path directly.
/about/ /#visit 301
/about /#visit 301
/spa-service/ /contact.html 301
/spa-service /contact.html 301
/san-diego-county-ca/ / 301
/san-diego-county-ca / 301
